# 2. Target users and roles

## 2.1 Student member

A verified student can:
- Create and manage a profile.
- Add skills, tags, portfolio items, work preferences, and availability.
- Browse and search requests.
- Create requests for help.
- Receive matching request alerts.
- Offer to help with requests.
- Comment on or respond to a request in a structured way.
- Message other students inside the platform.
- Accept or be selected for a job.
- Mark work as delivered and confirm completion.
- Leave the required rating for a completed job.
- See their verified reputation and work statistics.
- Connect with other students, subject to privacy controls.
- Report, block, or mute another member.

## 2.2 Administrator / moderator

An administrator can:
- Manage approved email domains.
- Manage university campuses, departments, programmes, and semester options.
- Manage skill categories and tags.
- View and manage user reports.
- Review suspicious accounts, requests, offers, messages, and ratings.
- Handle job disputes and moderation cases.
- Suspend or restrict accounts when justified.
- Manage featured notices and platform announcements.
- View platform-level statistics without exposing private data unnecessarily.
- Review audit logs for sensitive administrative actions.

## 2.3 Future roles

Future versions may add university society accounts, department pages, verified faculty mentors, or university administration accounts. These are not required for the first release.

