# 9. Messaging and connections

## 9.1 In-app messages

Provide private one-to-one messaging for members who are allowed to contact one another.

Required features:
- Conversation list.
- Message history.
- Sent time.
- Read/unread indicator where practical.
- Basic text messages.
- Optional image/file attachments with strict file-size/type checks.
- Mute conversation.
- Block user.
- Report message/conversation.
- Job-linked conversation context when messaging about a request/job.

Do not reveal a user's private email address simply because someone sends them a message. Do not require users to move to WhatsApp to complete the platform workflow.

## 9.2 Connections

Users may send and accept connection requests. A connection list can help students remember people they have worked with or want to network with.

Connections must be optional and must not be required to post a request, make an offer, or message about a job.

## 9.3 Community/help interactions

The product may include a lightweight help/community area for questions such as:
- “Can someone explain inheritance in Java?”
- “Which course should I prepare for next semester?”
- “Anyone looking for a project teammate?”

Keep this area focused on university help and skill sharing. Do not turn the app into a general-purpose social network. Requests with a clear deliverable should use the main Request system so the job/review workflow remains consistent.

