# 14. Data model / database entities

Design a relational database with appropriate foreign keys, indexes, uniqueness constraints, and access rules. Exact naming can differ, but the concepts below must exist.

Suggested entities:

1. **users** — user ID, normalized institutional email, verification status, auth provider ID, account status, created date, deleted date, last active, profile visibility settings.
2. **institutions** — institution name and approved email domains.
3. **campuses** — campus records linked to institution.
4. **departments** — department records linked to institution/campus where needed.
5. **programmes** — optional degree/programme list.
6. **user_profiles** — display name, bio, campus, department, programme, semester, image, work mode, optional gender preference fields, visibility settings.
7. **skills** — canonical skill tags and categories.
8. **user_skills** — many-to-many link between users and skills, optionally with self-described proficiency.
9. **portfolio_items** — user-created portfolio entries and attachments/links.
10. **availability_slots** — user-set available days and time ranges/time zone.
11. **requests** — owner, title, description, category, budget, work mode, helper preferences, status, created time, expiry time, selected helper/job reference.
12. **request_skills** — skill tags linked to each request.
13. **request_targets** — selected departments, semesters, campuses, and other target filters.
14. **request_alerts** — recipient, request, sent time, expiry time, read state; unique per recipient/request.
15. **offers** — request, offer creator, message, availability, status, created time.
16. **jobs** — accepted offer/request, requester, helper, status, accepted time, delivered time, completed time, cancellation/dispute reason.
17. **conversations** — participants and optional linked request/job.
18. **messages** — sender, conversation, content, attachment metadata, sent/read timestamps.
19. **reviews** — job, reviewer, reviewee, star rating, optional comment, created time, moderation status; unique per job/reviewer.
20. **connections** — requester user, target user, connection status, timestamps.
21. **blocks** — blocker and blocked user.
22. **reports** — reporter, reported object/user, reason, details, status, admin resolution.
23. **notifications** — message/job/security/connection notifications distinct from expiring request alerts.
24. **admin_audit_logs** — administrator, action, target, reason, timestamp.
25. **account_deletion_records** — minimal restricted record for deletion, retention, re-registration, and anti-abuse policy.

Use soft deletion/anonymization only where required by the privacy policy. Apply data retention rules rather than retaining everything indefinitely.

