# 15. Business rules that must be enforced

These are non-negotiable invariants:

1. Only exact approved university email domains can register.
2. Initial allowed domain is `@numl.edu.pk`; `@gmail.com` and all other unapproved domains are rejected.
3. Email ownership must be verified by OTP before the account becomes active.
4. One active account per normalized university email.
5. A public request has a maximum 24-hour active lifetime.
6. A matching request alert stays in the Request Alerts inbox for 12 hours, then disappears; the actual request is not deleted by this alert expiry.
7. Requests use explicit status values and server-controlled state transitions.
8. Only the request owner can accept an offer.
9. Accepting an offer creates one job and changes the request to Processing.
10. A Processing request is removed from the public Active feed.
11. If the selected helper declines/cancels and the request has time remaining, return it to Active with the original expiry time; otherwise mark it Expired.
12. A normally Completed job must have a required star rating from the requester; written comment is optional.
13. One completed job creates exactly one verified helper review in the first release.
14. Reviews cannot exist without a valid job record.
15. A user cannot review themselves or review the same job more than once.
16. Profile statistics are calculated from verified database records, not manually entered.
17. Public contact details and payment account identifiers are private by default.
18. Payment is arranged directly between users; the platform does not hold money or offer escrow in the first release.
19. Block/report and moderation tools must be available.
20. Important account, security, job, and message notifications are not removed by the 12-hour request-alert expiry rule.

