# 20. Important user journeys to implement and test

## Journey A — new student registration
1. Student enters `student@numl.edu.pk`.
2. System accepts the domain and sends OTP.
3. Student enters correct OTP.
4. Student completes profile.
5. Student reaches the request feed.
6. A `@gmail.com` user is rejected before account activation.

## Journey B — create a request
1. Student opens Create Request.
2. Adds title, description, skill tags, department/semester/campus targets, gender preference if desired, work mode, and budget.
3. Posts request.
4. Request appears in the active feed with a 24-hour countdown.
5. Matching students receive one request alert each.
6. Each alert expires from the Request Alerts inbox after 12 hours.

## Journey C — offer help and get selected
1. A matching student opens the request.
2. Reviews requester details and offers help with a short message.
3. Requester sees offers and opens profiles.
4. Requester selects one helper.
5. Job record is created.
6. Request changes to Processing and disappears from the public active feed.
7. Both users can chat in-app.

## Journey D — successful completion and review
1. Helper marks work Delivered.
2. Requester checks the work.
3. Requester submits required star rating and optional written comment.
4. Job becomes Completed.
5. Request disappears from active feed permanently.
6. Helper gets one verified review and updated statistics.
7. Counts remain consistent: each normally completed job has one required rating.

## Journey E — helper cancels during processing
1. Request is Processing with a selected helper.
2. Helper declines/cancels or requester ends the selection.
3. If original 24-hour expiry has time remaining, request returns to Active with the remaining time.
4. If expiry has passed, request becomes Expired.
5. Interested users may be notified that it is active again.

## Journey F — delete and re-register
1. User opens Settings → Delete Account.
2. User receives OTP at their university email.
3. Correct OTP is required.
4. Public profile is hidden, sessions revoked, and active requests handled safely.
5. Later, same university email may be verified and used to create a new account.
6. New public profile starts with zero public stats; minimal prior anti-abuse records remain restricted according to the privacy policy.

## Journey G — report and block
1. User reports a request, message, or profile.
2. Report appears in admin queue.
3. User can block the reported member.
4. Admin reviews and records an action/reason.
5. Report status is updated and relevant users are notified where appropriate.

